\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Two-stage training. Stage~1 trains the ConvNeXt (stages 1--5) and the ML-Decoder end-to-end with ASL. Stage~2 copies these weights (dashed lines) and fine-tunes all of them; the decoder is kept, and ASL is joined by a triplet loss against a cross-batch memory bank with entropy-gated anchors (Eqs.~(\ref {eq:entropy})--(\ref {eq:triplet})), giving $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {ASL}}+\lambda \,\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {tri}}$. The bank, gate and triplet term are used only during training.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
